+/* --- the compared chip: caption over the pill group (G1: 40px, pills 18px) - */
+/* While comparing, every other chip keeps its whole caption and a short
+   value: its floor (--chip-min) is measured by graph.js (fitCompareRow) and
+   it grows back toward its M4 width into whatever room is left. The pill
+   chip keeps its content width until the row is full; then it gives way in
+   measured steps (fix round 1, R02-M3): tighter gaps and no chevron
+   (.is-tight), each pill's shorter form ("Goldman", "2025–26"; the whole
+   name in its title), and only then an ellipsis. It was the other way round:
+   64px chips reading "In… B…" while the pills kept their names. */
